Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: iris: use visible encoder input size on gen1

The V4L2 source format includes storage alignment (720 becomes 736 rows).
HFI input frame size needs the visible dimensions retained by iris_venc,
as in the gen2 encoder. Keep decoder configuration unchanged.

On SM8250, a 1280x720 NV12 test compressed each 45-row band to 44 rows
and appended 16 green rows. This correction restores all 15 boundaries.
Base: Linux v7.2.6 + upstream 6f62dcefd249 + Armada fd0ed0f.
License: GPL-2.0-only, matching the modified kernel source.

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c
index 7674b47a..46785a65 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c
@@ -793,6 +796,13 @@ static int iris_hfi_gen1_set_resolution(struct iris_inst *inst, u32 plane)
 		fs.buffer_type = HFI_BUFFER_INPUT;
 		fs.width = inst->fmt_src->fmt.pix_mp.width;
 		fs.height = inst->fmt_src->fmt.pix_mp.height;
+		if (inst->domain == ENCODER) {
+			/* Storage dimensions include NV12 alignment padding. Firmware
+			 * needs the visible input dimensions, as on the gen2 path.
+			 */
+			fs.width = inst->enc_raw_width;
+			fs.height = inst->enc_raw_height;
+		}
 
 		ret = hfi_gen1_set_property(inst, ptype, &fs, sizeof(fs));
 		if (ret)
